      "content": "Your symptoms could indicate a worsening infection which may require prompt treatment beyond home remedies. Shivering and being run down are significant as they can suggest your body is fighting an infection systemically. Strong antibiotics are not always appropriate for fungal infections like ringworm, and you could inadvertently cause a drug-resistant bacterial infection. It is strongly advised to seek professional medical advice promptly. In the meantime, keep the area clean, use over-the-counter hydrocortisone for itching only, and monitor your symptoms closely. If your condition deteriorates, seek urgent medical attention. Remember, self-treatment can lead to more serious health consequences.",
